    "body": "## Summary\n\nUse `tmem.free(tmem_ptr, num_columns=self.tmem_alloc_cols)` in the SM100 D256 MXFP8 dQ and dK/dV kernels instead of overwriting the allocator's private column counter.\n\nWhen the allocator carries that counter as a DSL value, assigning a Python integer inside the release warp branch changes its carried structure and compilation fails with `CONTAINER_STRUCTURE_CHANGED`. The explicit-count API preserves the allocator state and releases the same number of columns. No public signature or synchronization changes.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Reduced two-CTA SM100 compile test, with allocation and release in separate runtime warp branches: the original assignment reproduces the 3-to-2 structure error; explicit-count release passes and emits matching 512-column allocation/deallocation.\n- Changed-file pre-commit hooks passed (Black, notebook formatting and SPDX).\n- Python syntax checks and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Full `test/python/sdpa/frost/test_sdpa_bwd_prepared_mxfp8.py` GPU validation is pending. This remains draft until the affected suite is verified.\n\n## Before submitting\n\n- [x] I agree to license this contribution under LICENSE.txt.\n- [x] I ran the changed-file pre-commit hooks.\n- [x] I reviewed the applicable Hard Rules. This change adds no host work, launch, allocation or synchronization.\n- [ ] Required labels: `cat-bugfix`, `area:frost`, `orig-nv-eng` (maintainer assistance may be needed).\n\n## Affected area\n\nFE OSS kernels or CuTeDSL.\n",
